tolerance: width <= delta uses TOL_W = 1e-12; implementation agreement |dA| <= 1e-10

Operational definition of 'suppressing the convention':
  package convention = 'empty arm = failure': P_arm(0) = 0 for both arms, so any replication
  with K = 0 or K = N contributes 0 to the joint assurance.
  suppressed convention = remove that override and evaluate the empty arm (m = 0, x = 0)
  by its prior-only credible interval Beta(a, b) with the same formula as every other arm:
  P_arm(0) = 1 if prior width <= delta (+TOL_W), else 0. Terms with m >= 1 are unchanged.
  The assurance can therefore change only if the prior-only width of an empty arm is <= its
  target, and by at most P(K in {0, N}).

